as anime fans we all know that the  medium is full of inspirational stories  a lot of the timeless classics and the  perpetual favorites all involve one of  the most classic storyline roots  the underdog story a lot of our beloved  heroes and protagonists go through one  hell of a challenge and the journey to  get to being the strongest is a long and  treacherous path everyone takes  different routes to get there we have  stuff where a protagonist goes from a  weakling to the most powerful being in  the universe throughout the course of a  season or multiple ones then we have the  one that's becoming more and more common  where the protagonist gets some  overpowered goods and practically  becomes an  in-universe god in the span of an  episode or two regardless here are the  main top characters that  embody the saying zero to hero we'll be  changing things up a little bit and  we're featuring  seven characters this time not doing it  in a countdown format oh before we get  started i'd like to say that nothing  would make me more happier than to see  this channel grow and have a lot more  subscribers as time goes by so with that  i'd encourage you to subscribe to this  channel and hit that notification bell  we're always looking to shake things up  here and i've got something very big  prepared for our next milestone  just be ready for it one last thing  spoilers are going to come out of this  list so  you have been warned  now when i think about a guy who turns  from loser to overpowered in just one  night  isakai leads come to mind with one of  the most notorious  examples of this in modern anime kicking  things off hajime nagumo there's really  not much to explain for hajime  especially if you're someone who watched  ari fiuretta i mean the title of the  show literally has the subtitle  from commonplace to the world's  strongest what happens when an issac  loser gets thrown into the abyss and  into certain death well desperation can  be one hell of a motivator  and with nothing to lose and the fire of  vengeance keeping him going  hajime manages to fight his way out of  the labyrinth a much more powerful  person than before  in the span of a couple of episodes he's  pretty much become the most overpowered  character in the ari furetta universe  he did have to go down and dirty though  but the challenges inside the labyrinth  that had him on death's door several  times were the last tangible hurdles for  him boasting an unmatched arsenal  incredible physical skills and a harem  of humans and monster girls that would  put naofumi to shame  hajime comes out virtually a god told  you the power to transmute is one of the  most broken ones when used to its full  potential  [Music]  let's continue with the shonen hero for  a change how about sooner  from hitman reborn  started off a useless kid who couldn't  talk to girls to save his life  and in the end a badass mafia boss of  the vongola and all it took was a  journey started by his meeting with  reborn  the cool part about tsuna is that his  journey to badass is something that gets  spread out throughout the series run  it's not as blatant and in your face as  a lot of shonen manga heroes journeys to  go from underdog to the strongest being  in the universe  but it is there we know what the dying  will bullets do to him but i actually  find more weight in his character growth  in the daily life segments  you see tsuna's development is a joy to  watch we were given those developments  in subtle doses and eventually  he overcomes his shell and becomes the  best ally you can have in times of  difficulty just look at the feats of  bravery that he's done without the need  for bullets  as mafia boss he's also an incredible  character that blows pretty much  everyone out of the water by the time  the series is done he's not the last  we'll see if shown in manga leads on  this list  so stay tuned  speaking of shonen heroes i think of  parasite shinichi  yeah shinichi is not a shonen hero  parasite's actually a seinen title from  way back  but still the point stands that he's a  success story of someone starting off  weak and then becoming strong  human monster fusions are some of the  most powerful beings in anime especially  when the two beings maintain their  individual wills and work together just  ask this guy  he goes from standard teenager to  parasite nightmare through his fated  meeting with migi who knew that a human  and a parasite working together would be  the crux to turning the tides of the war  against these aliens  the two work together and  single-handedly go through a gauntlet of  some of the toughest aliens in the enemy  side  in turn we get some of the best fight  scenes that the series has to offer  from many score fights to the final one  against gothor it's a perfect example of  characters starting out with teeth  clenched teamwork and a general low  standing on the power level scale and  evolving into becoming one of the  strongest forces in the series  not just physically but mentally as well  however it's the shared will and heart  that the two share which i'd consider  the most powerful asset that they have  [Music]  caught in a similar scenario to hajime  we have rimuru tempest  reincarnated as a slime he goes to the  same trials as the previous isakai hero  but instead of transmutation powers he  gets the ability to assimilate with  other creatures that he eats so what we  have here is pretty much a super version  of kirby and you can see where we're  going with this right all your powers  combined in the form of the most  powerful slime in the universe other  isekai leads just stand  no chance let me ask what's your answer  to an infinitely scaling slime god the  future is limitless for rimaru the  amazing part of it is that rimaru wasn't  even aware of his power at first just  look at his list of abilities on the  wiki and add on the fact that he's  pretty much immortal and we have one of  the most dramatic  zero-to-hero stories out there  is there anybody that embodies the  concept of going from weakling  to badass like ganeche does starting off  as a meek and weak student his life  takes a huge turn when he gets  transformed into a gould now things  won't come  easy and he refuses to accept his new  identity for quite a while  however when push comes to shove he  finally accepts his power and completely  destroys jason in one of the most badass  moments in season one eventually he  becomes some sort of mythological figure  and by the end of the series  it simply emphasizes how big of a  nightmare he's become  the thing about garniki is that instead  of becoming a straight-up heroic badass  he becomes more of an anti-hero as he  grows stronger  kind of like hajime from much earlier  how can we not have naruto in the list  his entire series is built and premised  on the ostracized kid dreaming big and  going from bumbling idiot to one of the  legendary figures responsible for the  village's legacy going forward what  makes naruto the series such a joy to  watch is that it's a slow  long and tough journey to see the  underdog create bonds  change people and find strength both  physically and emotionally some may  argue that the specific road to become  the celebrated hero of the village  concluded with the battle with pain but  naruto still went on and got some  at the end of it all we have one of the  greatest leaders that gonoh has ever  seen  strong enough with his fighting  abilities and the uncanny ability to  turn the edgiest people good with the  classic talk no jitsu yep  it seems that naruto is just the person  taylor made for a list like this  so how do you top off the list of zero  to hero stories  by transcending humanity such is the  case with who we're capping this list  off with  madoka  [Music]  for a series called madoka magicka our  main character sure spends  90 of the series being useless that's  not exactly an understatement and her  uselessness actually ties into the plot  and how it develops very nicely i could  probably do a long essay on the genius  of the series  but let's focus on the main character  for now you see that magical girl at  times she rocks in the opening  nowhere to be seen in all but the last  episode of the show madoka herself  spends the entire series crying  moping and questioning the intricacies  and nature of life and all of those  things  then the last episode comes and madoka  comes back with a vengeance  making her wish she transcends all human  boundaries and ascends to a higher plane  of existence  embodying the concept of fighting  witches madoka becomes god  quite literally rewriting the world not  even the biggest of her feats  as she goes back and ahead in time to  purify witches and changing the very  laws of the world  now that's a big swing in power if you  ask me  [Music]  that more or less wraps up this list  when making this list i decided to add  some more qualifiers which could explain  why some characters didn't make it to  the list backstory weakness disqualifies  characters so no sight armor despite the  huge leap in power characters holding  back or being misevaluated also get  disqualified from the list so sorry  ayato amagiri and tatsu yoshiba  although tatsuya himself is arguable  with those in mind do you think anyone  else could have quantified for this list  what do you think of me using this new  lucifer format instead of doing it in a  countdown form let your voices be heard  and start some discussions on the  comments section  for now that's gotta do it and i hope to  see you next time in the next video  don't forget to subscribe and hit that  sweet bell button so you can be the  first in line next time  you
 

